{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>A portion like the portion they shall eat.</b> This teaches that they divide the skins and the flesh of the sin-offering goats. One might say even regarding things that do not come on account of the festival, such as the daily offerings, the additional offerings of Sabbath, vows, and freewill offerings — therefore Scripture says: <b>Beside what he sells on the fathers.</b> Apart from what the fathers sold in the days of David and Samuel, when the watches were fixed and they sold to one another: 'You take your watch and I will take my watch' (there)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:33.311586017Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}